  data:  # ce9d
    kind: invariant  # ce9d
    title: "IoPrimitive.kind is written under three rules — the callee's construct (rust), whether a VALUE supplies its owner (python/cpp/scala/WI-komun), and what the analyzer stamps (java/kotlin) — and every consumer that branches on it needs the second"  # ce9d
    status: violated  # ce9d
    priority: 2  # ce9d
    parent:  # ce9d
    tags:  # ce9d
    - axis  # ce9d
    - io_boundary  # ce9d
    - catalogue  # ce9d
    - verify_claims  # ce9d
    isbefore: []  # ce9d
    duplicate_of: []  # ce9d
    not_duplicate_of: []  # ce9d
    pr_ref:  # ce9d
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-23 by the fundamental concept audit of IoPrimitive.kind (dev d917e02282).\nWrite-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-io-primitive-kind_09232026.md\nInstruments + 21 surveys: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kind_audit_09232026/\n\nTHE FIELD HAS NO DEFINITION, AND THE CATALOGUES STATE THREE, IN THEIR OWN WORDS:\n  R3 \"what the analyzer stamps\":  java.yaml:169 (\"Static methods, catalogued\n      method-kind ... java's analyzer stamps call_construct=method on every\n      selector-expression call\"), kotlin.yaml:156 (\"the analyzer emits them as\n      function-kind calls, so they are catalogued as functions\")\n  R2 \"owner named, no value receiver\": cpp.yaml:96 (\"Static member functions,\n      hence function-kind\"), scala.yaml:129 (companion factories, \"no value\n      receiver\"), python.yaml Path.cwd / datetime (INV-nular, INV-fugus),\n      test_associated_fn_kinds.py (\"A receiverless callee must not be catalogued\n      as a method\"), WI-komun (\"methods: means called on an instance whose type\n      must be known; a named global is resolved by NAME\")\n  R1 \"what the callee is\": rust.yaml:405 (\"catalogued as a method because that\n      is what it IS\"), and INV-pimir's statement (\"IoPrimitive.kind names the\n      construct of the DEFINITION\")\nScala holds two rules in one merged catalogue: its own Source.fromFile is R2,\nand the java.nio.file.Files statics it inherits via _CATALOG_PARENTS are R3.\n\nEVERY CONSUMER THAT BRANCHES ON IT NEEDS R2:\n  verify_claims method_starved_modules route 1 (joins to call_construct) and route 2\n  (function names = matchable without a stamp); io_boundary gate_named_entry (method\n  rows need receiver verification); the untyped-receiver disclosures (method rows are\n  \"reached through a receiver\"); io_boundary.py:1161, the INV-nizom arm (drops\n  function rows when the stamp is method and the slot is multi-candidate).\nAnd the starvation gate's own premise is false on the main path: with a definite\nmodule slot, `_qualified_rows` and the module filter never read kind at all.\n\nMEASURED CONSEQUENCES (arm A shipped vs arm B = rows with no value receiver\nre-kinded to function; nothing else differs):\n  - JS `process` classified-yet-starved on 6/9 JS-bearing repos (filed separately\n    as the INV-fugus family item).\n  - java: R3 is LOAD-BEARING through the INV-nizom join. Re-kinding statics loses\n    41 classifications (jedis 160->124, petclinic -3, gatling -2), because java emits\n    a multi-candidate slot for wildcard imports and stamps method on qualified statics.\n  - scala/kotlin: re-kinding drops untyped-receiver disclosures, and in sbt 76 of the\n    297 dropped are REAL Files./System./Instant. calls whose qualifier the analyzer\n    dropped (WI-kilap; explicit imports too), so the disclosure is their only signal.\n  - swift: 16 constructor rows are keyed methods and can never match (INV-gujoh\n    discussion).\n\nPROPOSED STATEMENT, NOT ADOPTED (two shipped rulings collide: WI-komun + INV-nular's\ntest say R2, INV-pimir's statement says R1; the owner decides): `methods:` iff the\ncallee's owner is supplied at the call site by a VALUE whose type must be inferred;\n`functions:` iff the owner is named at the call site (module, namespace, type,\ncompanion object, named global) or there is none; `attributes:` iff read, not called.\n\nSEQUENCING, MEASURED: the JVM re-kind waits on (a) the INV-nizom arm no longer reading\na `method` stamp as receiver evidence and (b) the kotlin/scala static-qualifier drop.\nSwift waits on boundary adjudication. JS process and python ctypes.cdll are\nunconstrained. WI-fazad (declare the enum) should carry whatever axiom is adopted."  # ce9d
    fields:  # ce9d
      statement: "A catalogue row's kind is a property of the primitive, stated one way in every catalogue: methods iff the callee's owner is supplied at the call site by a value whose type must be inferred; functions iff the owner is named at the call site or there is none; attributes iff read, not called. It never encodes what one analyzer stamps."  # ce9d
      root_cause: "No definition was ever written (WI-fazad: undeclared bounded enum), so each catalogue tuned kind to make its own analyzer's call_construct stamp pass the construct-x-kind joins (method_starved_modules route 1; the INV-nizom arm of lookup_with_module). The value therefore encodes the analyzer, not the primitive; java.yaml and kotlin.yaml say so in their notes."  # ce9d
- op: discuss  # 6123
  at: '2026-09-23T18:43:33Z'  # 6123
  by: agent  # 6123
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6123
  clock: 2  # 6123
  nonce: '6123'  # 6123
  message: "PANEL RESULT 2026-09-23 (owner convened a 3-seat panel: axis-design purist, verdict-soundness adjudicator, polyglot catalogue author; independent, read-only). UNANIMOUS: R2. NOT YET RATIFIED BY THE OWNER.\n\nAXIOM AS REFINED BY THE PANEL (all three moved it off the call site, and onto the row):\n  A row's kind says how the primitive is reached from the row's own `module`: methods iff it is called on an INSTANCE (a value) of `module`; functions iff it is called on `module` itself (namespace, package, type, companion object, named global) or has no owner; attributes iff it is read on `module`, not called.\n  Decision procedure (catalogue-author seat): if `module.name(...)` in the language's own qualifier syntax (`module(...)` for a constructor) is a valid call, it is a function; if a value of type `module` must precede `.name`, it is a method; if neither holds, the `module` string is wrong.\n  The purist seat's reason for dropping the audit's \"at the call site\" phrasing: ADR-0051 §1 says the module key \"is not a property of the call site\", and the sibling field must not reintroduce that leak.\n\nWHY R1 AND R3 LOST (all three seats, each verified independently):\n  - R1 has no row that needs it. rust.yaml's \"what it IS\" note sits on Instant::elapsed(&self), a method under R2 as well. Rust's associated fns are all functions:, pinned by test_associated_functions_are_function_kind. R1 exists only in INV-pimir's wording.\n  - R3 cannot be a property of a row that two analyzers read: _CATALOG_PARENTS gives scala and kotlin java's rows, and typescript loads the javascript YAML. The WI-komun -> WI-kikar sequence is R3 failing when an analyzer changed.\n  - Every branching consumer states R2 in its own docstring: gate_named_entry, untyped_receiver_sites (\"a function-kind primitive is not reached through a receiver at all\"), analyzer_disclosure.py:252.\n\nCORRECTION TO THE AUDIT (soundness seat, verified by reading; I have not re-run it): re-kinding JVM statics does NOT silence the 76 sbt sites. unknown_receiver_scope (verify_claims.py ~3707) does not read kind, and its caveat attaches whenever the count is > 0, so the verdict stays confirmed_with_caveats. What is lost is the boundary-scoped NAMING of those sites (a precision loss under ADR-0046), not the caveat. The write-up and the WI-kilap note overstated this.\n\nNEW FINDINGS FROM THE PANEL (not verified by me):\n  - kotlin.yaml ~103: the kotlin.io.FilesKt rows fit neither kind. No Kotlin value has type FilesKt, and FilesKt.readText(f) is not valid Kotlin, so the module string is wrong.\n  - The swift-nio-and-log overlay (~69-122) lists constructors under methods: and keys some on NIOSSL, which is a module, not a type.\n  - The python getattr_static sweep, extended to module and instance owners (probe: scratchpad/panel_author/probe.py): 601 of 602 resolvable rows conform. The only failure is ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary.\n  - Two gaps R2 does NOT close (soundness seat): (1) route 1 of method_starved_modules is still a proxy, since one method-stamped edge, even into an uncatalogued static (scala exitValue), satisfies the whole module; (2) a false all-clear on an unmatched call is prevented today only by module_completeness, which exists only in javascript, rust and python.\n\nORDER AGREED BY ALL THREE SEATS:\n  1. Adopt the axiom. Declare the axis: registry + helper replacing the literal \"method\"/\"function\" checks + drift linter + property test, plus a SHRINK-ONLY allowlist of the shipped rows that break it, each naming its blocker.\n  2. Re-kind JS process.on/send (to function) and process.cwd (attribute -> function), and python ctypes.cdll.LoadLibrary (INV-dihun).\n  3. Adjudicate the swift constructor rows' boundaries (INV-gujoh) before any re-kind there.\n  4. Stop the INV-nizom arm (io_boundary.py:1161) reading a method stamp as receiver evidence. Acceptance: jedis stays at 160 in the A/B.\n  5. WI-kilap, including its explicit-import half.\n  6. Re-kind the JVM statics; re-run measure.py.\n  7. Rewrite INV-pimir's statement and the method_starved_modules docstring premise; WI-fazad carries the declaration.\nWHAT WOULD REOPEN IT: after step 4, arm B still loses java classifications; OR >=1% of a row's matched call sites reach it both ways (unbound Path.read_text(p), obj.staticMethod()), which would need a fourth value or two fields; OR a consumer is shown to need \"member of a type\" regardless of static."  # 6123
