  message: "STEP 4 DONE (PR #1159): slot_names_one_owner() exempts a disjunctive module slot whose every entry names the same owner (java's wildcard slot, e.g. redis.clients.jedis.System,...,java.lang.System) from the INV-nizom arm; cpp's #include set is still file context. Measured over 21 surveys: arm A (shipped) is IDENTICAL on all 21, so no shipped output changed. Arm B (JVM statics re-kinded) lost 41 classifications before and loses 0 now (jedis 160, petclinic 14, gatling 32 with one gained); the acceptance condition held. The ledger's JVM statics now name only WI-kilap as blocker. Next: step 5 (WI-kilap)."  # 06ce
- op: discuss  # c3e8
  at: '2026-09-23T23:23:47Z'  # c3e8
  by: agent  # c3e8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c3e8
  clock: 8  # c3e8
  nonce: c3e8  # c3e8
  message: "STEP 5 DONE (PR #1160, WI-kilap done): in kotlin and scala a static call now names its owner (the file's dotted import, else java.lang's closed list minus each language's shadows, never a project type). Classified calls: sbt 123->237, gatling 31->57, detekt 17->30, http4s 3->6. Of 28 verify-claims verdicts, one gained a flow (sbt host-secret-no-host-fs, 4->5, still violated). Residual filed as WI-jubim (Runtime.getRuntime().exec: kotlin/scala do not consume library signatures). FOUND WHILE PREPARING STEP 6: re-kinding the JVM statics exposes them to gate_named_entry's bare-name fallback. Arm B matched sbt's own now() as Instant.now and gatling's own readString() as Files.readString, both false. Java has no free functions, so step 6 also lists every re-kinded name in ambiguous_names, which keeps the no-context path exactly as it was."  # c3e8
